  "details": "Current behavior: When a self global collider is in contact with a Physbone where Self Collision is allowed, disabling Self Collision will still allow the global collider to collide until it is no longer in contact with the physbones.\n\nExpected behavior: The self global colliders should not collide with the Physbones when disabling Self Collision.\n\nCurrent behavior: When a self global collider is in contact with a Physbone where Self Collision is not allowed, enabling Self Collision won't allow the global collider to collide until it is no longer in contact with the physbones.\n\nExpected behavior: The self global colliders should collide with the Physbones when enabling Self Collision.\n\nHere's the avatar ID for testing: avtr_d34c9e59-4083-4433-bfa4-02a337132cd0",
